WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.493
It's early in the morning at 123 Dance Studio.

2
00:00:07.493 --> 00:00:12.218
Professional dancers are already in the practice rooms.

3
00:00:12.218 --> 00:00:17.088
Let's meet some of them!

4
00:00:17.087 --> 00:00:19.806
Kira is a ballet dancer.

5
00:00:19.806 --> 00:00:24.289
She will audition for a role in The Nutcracker soon.

6
00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.870
That's a famous Russian ballet.

7
00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.708
Ballet is difficult to learn.

8
00:00:30.708 --> 00:00:36.166
Ballet dancers must be flexible and strong.

9
00:00:36.166 --> 00:00:40.952
See how Kira stands on one foot and makes a full turn?

10
00:00:40.952 --> 00:00:45.370
She must hold her body really straight to do this turn.

11
00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:48.338
Her shoes have flat front ends.

12
00:00:48.338 --> 00:00:52.801
The flat ends help her balance on the tips of her toes.

13
00:00:52.802 --> 00:00:57.832
Female ballet dancers often wear tutus for performances.

14
00:00:57.832 --> 00:01:01.356
These are short skirts with many layers.

15
00:01:01.356 --> 00:01:07.154
They let dancers move their legs freely.

16
00:01:07.154 --> 00:01:11.788
Good luck with your audition, Kira!

17
00:01:11.788 --> 00:01:15.462
Jay teaches hip-hop dance.

18
00:01:15.462 --> 00:01:19.236
He also creates dances for singers' music videos.

19
00:01:19.236 --> 00:01:21.896
He sometimes performs too.

20
00:01:21.896 --> 00:01:26.682
He's practicing a dance for today's class right now.

21
00:01:26.682 --> 00:01:31.070
Jay's movements are quick and timed to the strong beats.

22
00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:35.318
Hip-hop dancers can use every part of their bodies.

23
00:01:35.318 --> 00:01:40.450
Jay dances in his everyday clothes and comfortable shoes.

24
00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:47.780
This helps him to move his body freely.

25
00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:50.716
It looks like class is about to start.

26
00:01:50.716 --> 00:01:55.555
Let's move on.

27
00:01:55.555 --> 00:01:58.839
Lisa and Mel are tap dancers.

28
00:01:58.839 --> 00:02:03.030
Tap dancers make loud taps on the floor with their feet.

29
00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:06.496
They make these noises with special shoes.

30
00:02:06.496 --> 00:02:11.353
The bottoms of the shoes have metal plates at the heel and toe.

31
00:02:11.353 --> 00:02:15.592
When the metal hits the floor, it makes a loud noise.

32
00:02:15.592 --> 00:02:20.677
Tap dance performances were popular in the early twentieth century.

33
00:02:20.677 --> 00:02:24.932
Back then tap dancers often performed to jazz.

34
00:02:24.932 --> 00:02:31.104
But now it can be performed to almost any kind of music.

35
00:02:31.104 --> 00:02:34.222
People still enjoy tap dance today.

36
00:02:34.222 --> 00:02:37.478
Stomp! Stomp! Tap-tap!

37
00:02:37.478 --> 00:02:43.485
Lisa and Mel can tap fast!

38
00:02:43.486 --> 00:02:47.151
Being a professional dancer is a difficult job.

39
00:02:47.151 --> 00:02:50.609
It takes years of training and hard work.

40
00:02:50.610 --> 00:03:02.238
But dancing is fun for everyone. Watch this!

